    "blogtextliquid_LBJgtB": {
      "type": "blogtextliquid",
      "custom_css": [],
      "name": "Blog Text Liquid",
      "settings": {
        "text_content": "<p>You put it on in the morning, carefully, and by 11am it is gone. Not faded. Gone. You did everything right: you sprayed your wrists, your neck, maybe even stepped through a cloud of it before heading out the door. And yet your coworkers cannot smell it, and you cannot smell it.</p><p>This happens to almost everyone, and the immediate reaction is to blame the fragrance bottle. But in nine out of ten cases, premature scent disappearance has nothing to do with the perfume itself and everything to do with how and where you applied it.</p>"
      }
    },
    "177868816090d620d4": {
